  "articleBody": "When you're looking for an AI SEO solution for your family law practice, it can feel overwhelming to compare options. Many providers might offer general SEO, but AI SEO is a different beast entirely. It's not just about getting your website to rank; it's about positioning your firm to be the answer when AI systems provide information to prospective clients. You need a partner who understands the nuances of family law content and the specific requirements for AI citation.\n\nLook for providers who emphasize content authority and an attorney-review workflow. Since family law involves sensitive and critical information like filing deadlines or custody standards, any AI-assisted content must be reviewed by a human lawyer for accuracy and compliance. A good solution will also focus on mapping searches by issue and jurisdiction—divorce, custody, property—to ensure your content is hyper-relevant. Additionally, they should be able to strengthen your attorney, location, and contact information, ensuring consistency across platforms that AI systems rely on to build an entity profile.\n\n### How to Compare Your Options\n\nWhen comparing AI SEO solutions, ask about their content generation process. Do they focus on original, reliable content, or just repackage generic AI output? What are their source and citation controls for legal information? A crucial point is how they handle updates—family law statutes and court rules change, so continuous monitoring is essential. Also, inquire about their technical SEO capabilities for site architecture and structured data, and how they report on both conventional organic traffic and AI-search visibility. The best partners will clearly explain which AI tools they use and how they detect errors, ensuring your firm's online presence is not only visible but also trustworthy and compliant.",
